Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Nicole Ann Belsley  M D  Reports To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Invasive ductal carcinoma  DCIS of right breast  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  TWO FOCI OF RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  PRESENT ON OPPOSITE SIDES OF THE BIOPSY CAVITY AND SCAR  THE SPAN FROM FOCUS TO FOCUS  ACROSS THE SCAR  IS 1 9CM  THE SPAN OF THE LARGEST INDIVIDUAL FOCUS IS 0 13CM  ONE FOCUS IS 0 2CM FROM THE ANTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  THE POSTERIOR RESECTION MARGINS IS FREE OF CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  2  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   3 FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  There is no evidence of invasive carcinoma  An E Cadherin stain is non contributory as the area of interest is not present on the slide  Dr  Koerner has reviewed the foci of ductal carcinoma in situ and concurs with the diagnosis  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  UNREMARKABLE SKIN  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a 740 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm simple mastectomy with a stitch designating 12 o clock  There is an REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm tan skin ellipse on the anterior surface including the nipple and areola complex and a 5 5cm linear scar on the 6 o clock end of the skin ellipse  Underlying the 6 o clock end of the skin   there is a 3 0cm in length linear defect of the adipose tissue  exposing the pink glistening lining of the biopsy cavity  The anterior surface of the specimen is inked blue and the posterior is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm biopsy cavity lined by smooth tan pink lining and surrounded by focal fat necrosis  In addition  there is firm fibrous tissue surrounding the biopsy cavity  up to 1 5cm  predominantly superior and anterior to the biopsy cavity abutting the blue inked margin at 6 o clock  The biopsy cavity is 0 2cm from the inferior  6 o clock  anterior margin  1 5cm from the underlying skin and posterior margin  and more than 2cm from all remaining margins  The remaining tissue is tan adipose tissue with scattered white fibrous areas  No lymph nodes are identified  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm white fibrous area  just lateral to the biopsy cavity and abutting the inferior margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity and inferior anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity and posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity and superior firm area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional biopsy cavity and inferior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous area  lateral to biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section away from biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of unremarkable tan skin strips  excised to a depth of 0 8cm  Representative sections are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Nicole Ann Belsley M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Nicole Ann Belsley M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Nicole Ann Belsley M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Paula Arnell M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION , Unknown.
