argin  and a long black stitch the lateral margin  The posterior margin is inked black  and the anterior blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm gray white stellate scar in the mid outer breast tissue which comes to 0 2cm of the posterior margin  Along the medial aspect of the scar are several firm gray white focally gritty nodules ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  The largest nodule comes to 3 2cm of the posterior margin  Abutting the scar along the lateral aspect is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm fairly well defined dense gray  white fibrous nodular area with cystic change and diffuse gray pink nodules averaging 0 2cm in greatest dimension  This nodular area comes to 0 1cm of the posterior margin  The remaining cut surface displays unremarkable fibrous cystic breast tissue  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Posterior margin closest to largest nodule medial to scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest nodule medial to scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Scar including posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodular area lateral to scar including posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four intact lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple intact lymph nodes  Received in formalin  labeled  additional superficial tissue left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of tan yellow fibrofatty tissue with no orientation  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable tan yellow fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  re excision left breast skin   is a circular strip of unremarkable tan pink skin with a maximal diameter of 11 0cm  and an internal diameter of 9 0cm  Representative cross sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically